WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00.500
S T O P

00:03.580 --> 00:06.500
Come and listen to a story about a man named Jed

00:06.500 --> 00:08.920
He pulled a mountain here, barely kept his family fed

00:08.920 --> 00:10.980
And then one day he was shot

00:10.980 --> 00:12.780
He found some food and up through the ground

00:12.780 --> 00:14.980
Called the bubbling glue

00:14.980 --> 00:16.740
Oil that is

00:16.740 --> 00:18.140
Black gold

00:18.140 --> 00:19.980
Texas teeth

00:19.980 --> 00:23.220
Well the first thing you know Jed's a millionaire

00:23.220 --> 00:25.760
Kid and folks said Jed move away from there

00:25.760 --> 00:28.120
Said California's the place he ought to be

00:28.120 --> 00:31.620
So they loaded up the truck and they moved to Beverly

00:31.620 --> 00:33.300
Hills that is

00:33.300 --> 00:34.760
Swimming pools

00:34.760 --> 00:36.760
Movie stars

00:36.760 --> 00:59.660
The Beverly Hillbillies

00:59.660 --> 01:08.500
The Big Bang Theory

01:08.500 --> 01:10.300
You see Duke? It's easy

01:10.300 --> 01:11.960
I just throw this stick out yonder

01:11.960 --> 01:14.000
You pick it up and fetch it back

01:14.000 --> 01:14.800
Okay

01:14.800 --> 01:17.040
Well we'll do it again

01:17.040 --> 01:18.540
Go on boy, get it

01:18.540 --> 01:22.340
Fetch it to me, fetch it, fetch it

01:22.340 --> 01:24.420
Alright I'll show you, just once more now

01:24.420 --> 01:25.920
You watch

01:25.920 --> 01:33.220
Catch on Duke?

01:33.220 --> 01:35.700
Catch on boy?

01:35.700 --> 01:38.360
Just once more

01:38.360 --> 01:40.360
Catch it Duke, get it

01:40.360 --> 01:46.800
Come on, get it

01:46.800 --> 01:50.200
Shucks

01:50.200 --> 01:51.700
You know something Uncle Jed?

01:51.700 --> 01:54.980
That there is a real dumb dog

01:54.980 --> 01:56.480
Well I don't think he's so dumb

01:56.480 --> 01:59.780
Yes really, he just learned you how to fetch sticks for him

01:59.780 --> 02:02.080
But the dog is the one that's supposed to do the fetching

02:02.080 --> 02:05.880
Why there's a fella down the street that has a dog that fetches sticks for him all day

02:05.880 --> 02:08.160
Well next time you want some sticks fetched

02:08.160 --> 02:10.460
Go down the street and let that dog fetch them

02:10.460 --> 02:12.960
You just don't care nothing about it

02:12.960 --> 02:14.060
I got it, I got it, I got it

02:14.060 --> 02:16.900
I got some top model cops out of here

02:16.900 --> 02:17.840
Jed

02:17.840 --> 02:19.940
Do you want some vendors today?

02:19.940 --> 02:21.280
I do Granny

02:21.280 --> 02:24.340
I've worked up a right smart appetite fetching sticks for old Duke

02:24.340 --> 02:27.140
Hey Jed, that's the trouble around here

02:27.140 --> 02:29.040
The critters are taking over

02:29.040 --> 02:33.080
Billy May has done made pets out of everything but my pickled turds

02:33.080 --> 02:35.180
What's we gonna do for middles?

02:35.180 --> 02:38.580
Hey, I remember something Mr. Drysdale told us when we first moved in here

02:38.580 --> 02:39.420
What's that?

02:39.420 --> 02:41.620
He said anytime Granny didn't feel like cooking

02:41.620 --> 02:44.000
There was some folks that had fetched food over to us

02:44.000 --> 02:46.300
Here in Beverly Hills?

02:46.300 --> 02:47.300
Yes ma'am

02:47.300 --> 02:50.200
All you gotta do is call them on the telephone and tell them what you want

02:50.200 --> 02:51.800
Mmm, no he's

02:51.800 --> 02:53.040
That's mighty neighborly

02:53.040 --> 02:54.940
What do you call her name, General?

02:54.940 --> 02:56.480
Let's see

02:56.480 --> 02:58.240
Cater

02:58.240 --> 03:00.140
We call her first name?

03:00.140 --> 03:01.980
It's a woman

03:01.980 --> 03:03.180
Beverly

03:03.180 --> 03:04.780
Beverly Caterer?

03:04.780 --> 03:06.080
Must be a widow woman

03:06.080 --> 03:07.580
She's the best cook Jed

03:07.580 --> 03:09.560
They have more time

03:09.560 --> 03:12.260
Well let's call up the widow and see what she's got cooking today

03:12.260 --> 03:13.720
Now just a minute Jed

03:13.720 --> 03:17.120
I want it made clear that I'm gonna do something for her in return

03:17.120 --> 03:19.660
Oh naturally we don't take charity

03:19.660 --> 03:25.640
Come on dude, let's try it again

03:25.640 --> 03:28.680
Oh hi there Miss Operator

03:28.680 --> 03:30.580
This here is Jed Clampett

03:30.580 --> 03:33.280
I'm wanting to call her Witticaterer

03:33.280 --> 03:35.280
Beverly is a Christian name

03:35.280 --> 03:37.620
I don't rightly know what her late husband was called

03:37.620 --> 03:41.080
Anyway, she's the one that cooks the food and takes it around to folks

03:41.080 --> 03:43.680
Yes ma'am, that's it

03:43.680 --> 03:45.020
Beverly Caterer

03:45.020 --> 03:47.820
Oh, caterers is it?

03:47.820 --> 03:49.000
More than one

03:49.000 --> 03:51.760
It's like the widows got some youngins to help with

03:51.760 --> 03:52.760
That's good Jed

03:52.760 --> 03:54.260
Most times they leave home

03:54.260 --> 03:55.260
Just when you...

03:55.260 --> 03:57.500
Oh thank you ma'am

03:57.500 --> 04:03.400
What was I just saying, Granny?

04:03.400 --> 04:05.980
I was saying that most times the youngins leave home

04:05.980 --> 04:07.540
Just about the time that you're...

04:07.540 --> 04:12.280
Well, howdy to you Miss Beverly Caterer

04:12.280 --> 04:13.980
This here is Jed Clampett

04:13.980 --> 04:15.920
Sounds like a right friendly woman

04:15.920 --> 04:18.820
Howdy Beverly, this here is Granny

04:18.820 --> 04:20.260
I'm a widow myself

04:20.260 --> 04:21.960
And I was just saying to Jed

04:21.960 --> 04:24.360
It's nice when the youngins stay home to help you

04:24.360 --> 04:27.360
So many times they leave just when you need them most

04:27.360 --> 04:33.100
I'll let you women folks talk about the biddle

04:33.100 --> 04:35.900
But first I just want to say if you ever need a fence mended

04:35.900 --> 04:37.740
Or a well dug or any heavy work at all

04:37.740 --> 04:38.980
You just call on Jethro and me

04:38.980 --> 04:39.980
Now here's Granny

04:39.980 --> 04:44.140
Beverly, what you got on the back of the stove this morning?

04:44.140 --> 04:46.180
I don't want to put you to no extra trouble

04:46.180 --> 04:47.180
Huh?

04:47.180 --> 04:50.920
Well me, I'm partial to baked possum

04:50.920 --> 04:54.120
But we'll take dowels or fatback or sowbelly

04:54.120 --> 04:56.460
Any kind of meat or pleasure is considerable

04:56.460 --> 04:59.460
What's that?

04:59.460 --> 05:00.460
Bunch of nuts

05:00.460 --> 05:02.960
Well, you can send them along

05:02.960 --> 05:06.740
I'll tell you right now the critters will get the bulk of them

05:06.740 --> 05:11.500
Now tell me something we can do for you honey

05:11.500 --> 05:12.500
Do what?

05:12.500 --> 05:22.580
Hello

05:22.580 --> 05:23.580
I declare Jed

05:23.580 --> 05:27.220
I never know anybody could turn nasty quicker than her

05:27.220 --> 05:29.700
What do I set her on?

05:29.700 --> 05:30.700
Hard to tell Jed

05:30.700 --> 05:35.620
A generous woman like her probably gets took advantage of a lot

05:35.620 --> 05:37.580
And tired to boot I reckon

05:37.580 --> 05:43.260
Uncle Jed, I can't learn this dumb old dog to fetch his stick

05:43.260 --> 05:45.660
Well Duke can't about to waste his time chasing a piece of wood

05:45.660 --> 05:46.660
He's hunting dog

05:46.660 --> 05:47.660
Well can I take him hunting then?

05:47.660 --> 05:49.300
I'd like to see him chase something

05:49.300 --> 05:50.300
Praise be

05:50.300 --> 05:53.620
That's an idea that might put some fresh meat on our table

05:53.620 --> 05:56.140
All right boy, it makes more sense than fetching a stick

05:56.140 --> 05:57.140
Especially to Duke

05:57.140 --> 05:58.620
Do you want to come along Granny?

05:58.620 --> 05:59.620
No

05:59.620 --> 06:01.700
I better stay here and guard my kitchen

06:01.700 --> 06:02.700
Okay

06:02.700 --> 06:03.700
Come on Duke, let's get the guns

06:03.700 --> 06:05.180
Guard your kitchen and get a shoe Granny

06:05.180 --> 06:07.500
Against scary critters, that's who

06:07.500 --> 06:09.100
They're beginning to take over

06:09.100 --> 06:10.100
Why I can't hardly

06:10.100 --> 06:17.300
That little rascal learned to open the icebox

06:17.300 --> 06:19.780
Then he's a rascal and a pickle paw paw

06:19.780 --> 06:24.020
Come back here you hairy little armadge

06:24.020 --> 06:31.900
Get your paw paw picking paws off of my pickle paw paw

06:31.900 --> 06:33.460
Howdy Miss Beverly

06:33.460 --> 06:34.620
It's me Jed Clampett

06:34.620 --> 06:38.420
Sound like you're in the right friendly mood again

06:38.420 --> 06:40.540
Jethro's going out to shoot us some fresh game meat

06:40.540 --> 06:43.700
And the monkey got him an icebox and Granny's right upset

06:43.700 --> 06:48.540
Now Beverly, could you spare us a jar of pickle paw paws?

06:48.540 --> 06:49.540
What's that?

06:49.540 --> 06:52.340
Why Miss Kater, I never

06:52.340 --> 06:53.340
Hello Miss Kater

06:53.340 --> 06:57.980
Hey Uncle Jed, you got Miss Kater being with us

06:57.980 --> 07:00.180
Such a good cook and friendly and generous gnot

07:00.180 --> 07:01.860
How about you Cortner?

07:01.860 --> 07:03.660
Get Ellie a new ma huh?

07:03.660 --> 07:04.980
I don't think so Jethro

07:04.980 --> 07:07.100
She's got a temper goes off just like that

07:07.100 --> 07:09.260
And when it does she turns plum nasty

07:09.260 --> 07:13.740
Matter of fact I'm beginning to wonder whether Miss Kater passed on natural or not

07:13.740 --> 07:16.140
That's an idea

07:16.140 --> 07:17.140
Come on dude

07:17.140 --> 07:21.540
How come you're toting so many guns in that shovel Jethro?

07:21.540 --> 07:23.820
Granny gave me strict orders not to come back empty handed

07:23.820 --> 07:27.140
I'm ready for anything to jumps, flies, runs or digs into the ground

07:27.140 --> 07:29.460
Good luck boy

07:29.460 --> 07:33.380
Oh gee thank goodness you're back

07:33.380 --> 07:36.420
I didn't want to disturb you at the meeting but your wife has been calling frantically

07:36.420 --> 07:39.820
Oh that woman gets hysterical over nothing, what's it now?

07:39.820 --> 07:42.340
Well it seems there's a kangaroo in your backyard

07:42.340 --> 07:44.900
You say the slightest little...

07:44.900 --> 07:45.900
What?

07:45.900 --> 07:49.500
Well a kangaroo, where did it come from?

07:49.500 --> 07:52.380
Australia, that's the only continent where

07:52.380 --> 07:55.700
Oh I know that, how did it get in my backyard?

07:55.700 --> 07:59.300
Well your wife was rather incoherent but Ravenswood said it's from the second national

07:59.300 --> 08:00.940
bank of Melbourne

08:00.940 --> 08:02.260
Second national bank?

08:02.260 --> 08:06.780
Oh that's where Gene Sandbloom was transferred to from...

08:06.780 --> 08:08.460
That explains his Christmas card

08:08.460 --> 08:10.660
May I share the humor of the situation chief?

08:10.660 --> 08:15.180
Well I sent him an alligator wallet so he said he was going to send me a kangaroo pouch

08:15.180 --> 08:16.180
Kangaroo pouch?

08:16.180 --> 08:17.180
On the whoop is it worth?

08:17.180 --> 08:18.180
Mr Sandbloom does have a sense of humor

08:18.180 --> 08:19.180
Yes we'll have the zoo pick it up, I'll call Margaret

08:19.180 --> 08:20.180
Mr Grisdale's office?

08:20.180 --> 08:21.180
Oh Ravenswood

08:21.180 --> 08:22.180
Uh huh

08:22.180 --> 08:23.180
Good I'll tell him

08:23.180 --> 08:24.180
Oh I'm sorry, I'm sorry

08:24.180 --> 08:25.180
I'm sorry

08:25.180 --> 08:26.180
I'm sorry

08:26.180 --> 08:27.180
I'm sorry

08:27.180 --> 08:28.180
I'm sorry

08:28.180 --> 08:29.180
I'm sorry

08:29.180 --> 08:30.180
I'm sorry

08:30.180 --> 08:31.180
I'm sorry

08:31.180 --> 08:32.180
I'm sorry

08:32.180 --> 08:33.180
Oh well it comes to Grisdale

08:33.180 --> 08:35.880
Oh and don't worry about the kangaroo the zoo will take care of it

08:35.880 --> 08:36.880
Right

08:36.880 --> 08:37.880
Tiddy-o

08:37.880 --> 08:41.980
Ravenswood has your wife under sedation and she's resting comfortably

08:41.980 --> 08:42.980
Oh good

08:42.980 --> 08:53.420
Here we are, a bit of mutton and Yorkshire pudding should hit the spot

08:53.420 --> 08:57.020
You may be from down under but we're all part of the empire

08:57.020 --> 09:02.020
Oh, Brett, the zoo must have already come for you.

09:06.020 --> 09:09.020
Oh, I'm gonna cook up a rabbit stew.

09:09.020 --> 09:12.020
Soon as Jeff roasts you to be one or two.

09:12.020 --> 09:17.020
Then we'll all sit down to the table and we'll eat, then we'll eat.

09:20.020 --> 09:21.020
Mmm.

09:21.020 --> 09:34.020
How you going, Granny?

09:34.020 --> 09:37.020
Kid, you can't so leave to go hunting, Ed?

09:37.020 --> 09:38.020
Yep.

09:38.020 --> 09:39.020
Well, he needn't have bothered.

09:39.020 --> 10:03.020
There's a jack rabbit out back that high.

10:03.020 --> 10:06.020
Now, you hold on, Jed Trampett.

10:06.020 --> 10:09.020
I tell you, I ain't touch the drop.

10:09.020 --> 10:14.020
And there is a giant jack rabbit out in our backyard, and it is this high.

10:14.020 --> 10:20.020
Granny, you and me has seen some good size jacks in our day, but not five foot tall.

10:20.020 --> 10:25.020
Kid, there's a lot of things we never seen back home that we are seeing out here.

10:25.020 --> 10:27.020
And that's one of them.

10:27.020 --> 10:33.020
A piano playing, ice box opener, Paw Paw Philford 8.

10:33.020 --> 10:45.020
All right, Granny, I'll go take a look at your jack rabbit.

10:45.020 --> 10:47.020
Come on, you can see for yourself.

10:47.020 --> 10:52.020
He can jump over this house, I tell you, in one hop.

10:52.020 --> 10:53.020
Whereabouts is he?

10:53.020 --> 10:55.020
I don't know.

10:55.020 --> 11:01.020
But sure as I live and breathe, he was sitting right there, five foot tall and looking me in the eye.

11:01.020 --> 11:02.020
Five foot tall, sitting, was he?

11:02.020 --> 11:03.020
Yes, he was.

11:03.020 --> 11:06.020
Where did that jack rabbit go?

11:06.020 --> 11:08.020
Well, why don't you look out front?

11:08.020 --> 11:10.020
Maybe hop door to house, just like you say.

11:10.020 --> 11:14.020
You think I'm talking nonsense, but you'll see, because I'll find him.

11:14.020 --> 11:15.020
What's all the sound about, Granny?

11:15.020 --> 11:16.020
Nothing.

11:16.020 --> 11:18.020
Don't tell her, Jed.

11:18.020 --> 11:20.020
I don't want her making a pet out of all that meat.

11:20.020 --> 11:24.020
I'll let her go in the kitchen and get out my biggest pot and start peeling taters.

11:24.020 --> 11:26.020
Lots of them.

11:26.020 --> 11:27.020
Here, Dad.

11:27.020 --> 11:28.020
Here, Dad.

11:28.020 --> 11:29.020
Here, Dad.

11:29.020 --> 11:31.020
Who's Dad, Paw?

11:31.020 --> 11:32.020
Never mind, Ellie.

11:32.020 --> 11:35.020
Just trying to keep your critters from pestering Granny.

11:35.020 --> 11:39.020
You got her so upset, she got into her jug, and now she's seeing visions.

11:39.020 --> 11:40.020
What kind of visions?

11:40.020 --> 11:42.020
Well, I reckon it's all right to tell you.

11:42.020 --> 11:45.020
Granny thinks she's seen a five foot jack rabbit.

11:54.020 --> 11:56.020
Howdy, Mr. Jack Rabbit.

11:57.020 --> 11:59.020
The weather's turned off real nice, ain't it?

11:59.020 --> 12:03.020
There's a mighty fine sober out there on the lawn if you want to fatten up.

12:03.020 --> 12:05.020
I mean, if you're hungry.

12:05.020 --> 12:08.020
But if you go away, there's somebody I want you to meet.

12:12.020 --> 12:14.020
I'll be right back.

12:18.020 --> 12:20.020
Jed, Jed, come on up and I found him.

12:20.020 --> 12:29.020
Come quick.

12:29.020 --> 12:32.020
Dad, Dad, I see him again, the giant jack rabbit.

12:32.020 --> 12:33.020
I bet you did.

12:33.020 --> 12:34.020
He's right out front.

12:34.020 --> 12:35.020
Come on, I'll show him to you.

12:35.020 --> 12:37.020
Maybe you better lay down, Spill.

12:37.020 --> 12:39.020
No, no, he'll get away again.

12:39.020 --> 12:41.020
All right, I'll take a look.

12:47.020 --> 12:48.020
See him, Dad?

12:48.020 --> 12:51.020
I lost my glasses, but he must be out there somewhere.

12:51.020 --> 12:53.020
Well, yeah, yeah, I see him.

12:53.020 --> 12:55.020
Is he out on the lawn eating clover?

12:55.020 --> 12:57.020
Red, big old pink jack rabbit.

12:57.020 --> 12:58.020
Pink!

12:58.020 --> 12:59.020
Don't get upset.

12:59.020 --> 13:00.020
There's other colors, too.

13:00.020 --> 13:03.020
There's a blue one, there's a green one.

13:03.020 --> 13:05.020
Here comes one with purple polka dots.

13:05.020 --> 13:07.020
I wish I could see him.

13:08.020 --> 13:10.020
What's that you say, Mr. Jack Rabbit?

13:10.020 --> 13:12.020
All right, I'll tell her.

13:12.020 --> 13:14.020
He says he thinks you ought to go in and lay there.

13:14.020 --> 13:18.020
Yeah, I think I better head, Jade.

13:19.020 --> 13:20.020
Ah, hi there, Miss Jade.

13:20.020 --> 13:21.020
Jethro!

13:21.020 --> 13:24.020
And you got a wonderful surprise.

13:24.020 --> 13:27.020
But why do you look so worried, noble beast?

13:27.020 --> 13:29.020
Because I can't find no good hunting place, that's why.

13:29.020 --> 13:31.020
Your granny gave the strict orders to bring home some meat.

13:31.020 --> 13:34.020
Jethro, food should never be a problem to people of your means.

13:34.020 --> 13:37.020
There are markets, supermarkets, caterers.

13:37.020 --> 13:39.020
Uncle Jed called that their Beverly caterer.

13:39.020 --> 13:41.020
He got Mean Mouth something awful.

13:41.020 --> 13:42.020
Mean Mouth?

13:42.020 --> 13:46.020
He says she's the nastiest tempered woman that ever answered a telephone.

13:46.020 --> 13:48.020
Well, Mr. Dryjess will hear of this.

13:48.020 --> 13:50.020
The bank has a substantial interest in Beverly caterers.

13:50.020 --> 13:51.020
You wait here.

13:51.020 --> 13:53.020
Well, hi there, Beverly.

13:53.020 --> 13:54.020
This is Jed Clampett.

13:54.020 --> 13:56.020
You sounded right pleasant again.

13:56.020 --> 13:58.020
Now, wait, ma'am.

13:58.020 --> 14:00.020
I ain't called to ask for bills.

14:00.020 --> 14:03.020
It's just that your granny's laying down with a right smart headache.

14:03.020 --> 14:05.020
I was wondering whether you could fix her poultice.

14:07.020 --> 14:09.020
Tell her to do what?

14:09.020 --> 14:13.020
Well, I don't hardly see how that could help a headache.

14:13.020 --> 14:15.020
Now, wait a minute, man.

14:15.020 --> 14:17.020
Don't go flying off the handle.

14:17.020 --> 14:19.020
I just... Hello? Hello?

14:21.020 --> 14:22.020
There are two ways about it.

14:22.020 --> 14:25.020
That woman has got a temper like a wet hornet.

14:28.020 --> 14:30.020
Hello, Beverly caterers?

14:30.020 --> 14:32.020
One moment, please.

14:32.020 --> 14:34.020
Hello.

14:34.020 --> 14:37.020
Have you spoken to a Mr. Jed Clampett today?

14:37.020 --> 14:39.020
What? What?

14:39.020 --> 14:41.020
Now, just a minute, young lady.

14:41.020 --> 14:43.020
What is your name?

14:43.020 --> 14:45.020
What do you mean, put in tape?

14:45.020 --> 14:47.020
Now, you put Mr. Tinsman on the phone

14:47.020 --> 14:49.020
and tell him it's Milburn Drysdale calling.

14:49.020 --> 14:52.020
The nastiest tempered young woman I ever spoke to.

15:04.020 --> 15:06.020
Jed! Jed, come quick!

15:06.020 --> 15:08.020
He's back again?

15:08.020 --> 15:10.020
He went outside there. Go look quick, Jed.

15:10.020 --> 15:11.020
Who's that, Granny?

15:11.020 --> 15:13.020
The giant jack rabbit.

15:13.020 --> 15:15.020
Oh, him again.

15:15.020 --> 15:17.020
All right, where's the jug?

15:17.020 --> 15:19.020
What jug?

15:19.020 --> 15:21.020
The jug that rabbit keeps coming out of.

15:21.020 --> 15:22.020
The jug gives me that headache.

15:22.020 --> 15:24.020
I ain't touched the jug.

15:24.020 --> 15:26.020
I busted my head running into them curtains.

15:26.020 --> 15:28.020
Yeah, sure.

15:28.020 --> 15:30.020
They'll do it all right.

15:30.020 --> 15:32.020
I gotta catch that giant jack rabbit.

15:32.020 --> 15:33.020
Where's my shotgun?

15:33.020 --> 15:35.020
Well, Jeffery's got it out hunting.

15:35.020 --> 15:38.020
Then we gotta catch a snare and put a snare out for him.

15:38.020 --> 15:40.020
Granny, wouldn't you rather lay back down

15:40.020 --> 15:42.020
and let me bring you a nice big cup of black coffee?

15:42.020 --> 15:44.020
Now, I'm gonna catch that big giant jack rabbit

15:44.020 --> 15:47.020
whether you help me or not, and I don't care.

15:47.020 --> 15:49.020
I'll help you. I'll help you.

15:49.020 --> 15:51.020
All right, now you get me a nice big stout rope

15:51.020 --> 15:53.020
and put some bait in there.

15:53.020 --> 15:55.020
Yeah, it'd take about two dozen carats

15:55.020 --> 15:57.020
for a rabbit that size.

15:57.020 --> 15:59.020
Now you're thinking straight.

15:59.020 --> 16:01.020
Yeah.

16:01.020 --> 16:03.020
This took me a while.

16:03.020 --> 16:05.020
All right, get going.

16:05.020 --> 16:07.020
The rest of the tension is about to be made.

16:07.020 --> 16:09.020
Yes. Now, give your Uncle Jed a message.

16:09.020 --> 16:11.020
Tell him that the young woman who was so rude on the telephone

16:11.020 --> 16:13.020
will arrive in person to offer her abject apologies.

16:13.020 --> 16:16.020
Yes. And tell Granny she needn't worry about food.

16:16.020 --> 16:18.020
The young lady will also bring with her a truck full of delicious

16:18.020 --> 16:21.020
piping hot vines and an assortment of tasty beverages,

16:21.020 --> 16:23.020
all of which will be offered at your pleasure.

16:23.020 --> 16:25.020
Yes.

16:25.020 --> 16:27.020
Have I anything else to say, Miss Hathaway?

16:27.020 --> 16:29.020
No, no, chief, I think you've said it all.

16:29.020 --> 16:31.020
That sure is gonna make Uncle Jed and Granny happy.

16:31.020 --> 16:33.020
Thank you, Mr. Dorsdale.

16:33.020 --> 16:35.020
Not at all. Glad to do it.

16:37.020 --> 16:39.020
Jethro,

16:41.020 --> 16:43.020
don't you think you could reward me

16:43.020 --> 16:45.020
for my efforts?

16:45.020 --> 16:47.020
Well,

16:47.020 --> 16:49.020
all I've got with me is a nickel and two pennies,

16:49.020 --> 16:51.020
but you can have that.

16:51.020 --> 16:53.020
There are other ways for a handsome young man

16:53.020 --> 16:55.020
to reward a young lady.

16:55.020 --> 16:57.020
There is?

16:57.020 --> 16:59.020
Yes. Tell me, do you enjoy kissing?

16:59.020 --> 17:01.020
Well, I like to kiss girls.

17:01.020 --> 17:03.020
Well, then,

17:03.020 --> 17:05.020
I'm going to close my eyes,

17:05.020 --> 17:07.020
and I want you to enjoy yourself.

17:11.020 --> 17:13.020
Go ahead, Jethro.

17:13.020 --> 17:15.020
Enjoy yourself.

17:15.020 --> 17:17.020
I am, huh?

17:17.020 --> 17:19.020
Get out of here, you shameless vixen!

17:19.020 --> 17:21.020
Yes, ma'am.

17:21.020 --> 17:23.020
Come on, dude.

17:23.020 --> 17:25.020
Thank you for the kiss.

17:25.020 --> 17:27.020
Now,

17:27.020 --> 17:29.020
let's see.

17:29.020 --> 17:31.020
If I were to tie another rope

17:31.020 --> 17:33.020
onto the bottom of that limb,

17:33.020 --> 17:35.020
pull it down,

17:35.020 --> 17:37.020
and then

17:37.020 --> 17:39.020
take my loop

17:39.020 --> 17:41.020
and put some carrots in it,

17:43.020 --> 17:45.020
howdy, Mr. Jackrabbit.

17:45.020 --> 17:47.020
Would you like to step into my kitchen?

17:49.020 --> 17:51.020
You ain't gonna get away from me again.

17:51.020 --> 17:53.020
No, I won't.

17:53.020 --> 17:55.020
You ain't gonna get away from me again,

17:55.020 --> 17:57.020
I can tell you that.

17:57.020 --> 17:59.020
Now,

17:59.020 --> 18:01.020
are you gonna come peaceable,

18:01.020 --> 18:23.020
or do I have to take you by force?

18:23.020 --> 18:25.020
Dad! Dad!

18:25.020 --> 18:27.020
Come and run in! Come and run in!

18:27.020 --> 18:29.020
Dad!

18:29.020 --> 18:31.020
Granny, what's the matter now?

18:31.020 --> 18:33.020
The giant Jackrabbit! I had him cornered,

18:33.020 --> 18:35.020
but he fist-forked me!

18:35.020 --> 18:37.020
Fist-forked you?

18:37.020 --> 18:39.020
Yes, he did! Now you go outside and

18:39.020 --> 18:41.020
belt him outside the door!

18:41.020 --> 18:57.020
Granny, where are you hiding them jugs?

18:57.020 --> 19:01.020
Oh, I'm gonna cook up a rabbit stew,

19:01.020 --> 19:05.020
and one giant rabbit will do more than do.

19:05.020 --> 19:07.020
Granny, you don't have to do no cooking.

19:07.020 --> 19:09.020
Like I said, Dr. Beverly Cater's

19:09.020 --> 19:11.020
gonna bring over a whole truckload

19:11.020 --> 19:13.020
of Vions and beverages.

19:13.020 --> 19:15.020
I ain't depending on nobody with a temper

19:15.020 --> 19:17.020
as bad as her.

19:17.020 --> 19:19.020
Besides, I don't need her Vions.

19:19.020 --> 19:21.020
For the next couple of weeks, we're gonna be

19:21.020 --> 19:23.020
eating high on the rabbit.

19:23.020 --> 19:25.020
Where'd you get all the rabbits?

19:25.020 --> 19:27.020
One rabbit, Jethro.

19:27.020 --> 19:29.020
One rabbit?

19:29.020 --> 19:31.020
He must be a whopper.

19:31.020 --> 19:33.020
There were those big mountain Jacks

19:33.020 --> 19:35.020
we used to see back home?

19:35.020 --> 19:37.020
Yeah.

19:37.020 --> 19:39.020
He put a pair of them in his pocket.

19:39.020 --> 19:41.020
In his pocket?

19:41.020 --> 19:43.020
Sure. He stands five feet tall,

19:43.020 --> 19:45.020
and he has a pocket, right?

19:47.020 --> 19:49.020
You don't believe me, do you?

19:49.020 --> 19:51.020
Oh, yes I do, Granny.

19:51.020 --> 19:53.020
No, you don't.

19:53.020 --> 19:55.020
Oh, Granny, I sure I do.

19:55.020 --> 19:57.020
No, you don't.

19:57.020 --> 19:59.020
All right, I don't believe you.

19:59.020 --> 20:17.020
I don't believe you.

20:17.020 --> 20:19.020
Mr. Tinsman, do I have to face

20:19.020 --> 20:21.020
Mr. Clampett all by myself?

20:21.020 --> 20:23.020
Yes, you do. You're the one who insulted him

20:23.020 --> 20:25.020
on the phone, and you're the one

20:25.020 --> 20:27.020
he'll expect an apology from.

20:27.020 --> 20:29.020
But he talked like a nut.

20:29.020 --> 20:33.020
Miss Billington, a man as rich as Mr. Clampett

20:33.020 --> 20:35.020
may talk like an eccentric,

20:35.020 --> 20:37.020
but never like a nut.

20:37.020 --> 20:39.020
I sure hope he'll forgive me.

20:41.020 --> 20:43.020
He'll forgive you.

20:43.020 --> 20:47.020
If he's anywhere between 15 and 95,

20:47.020 --> 20:49.020
he'll forgive you.

20:49.020 --> 20:55.020
I'll take the food out of the kitchen.

20:59.020 --> 21:01.020
Uh, is Mr. Clampett at home?

21:01.020 --> 21:03.020
I'm here, Clampett. Come right in.

21:03.020 --> 21:05.020
This little fella don't say much,

21:05.020 --> 21:07.020
but he's right smart.

21:07.020 --> 21:09.020
Mr. Clampett, I'm here to apologize

21:09.020 --> 21:11.020
about the way I spoke to you

21:11.020 --> 21:13.020
on the telephone earlier today.

21:13.020 --> 21:15.020
Oh, you're Beverly Caterers.

21:15.020 --> 21:17.020
Yes, sir.

21:17.020 --> 21:19.020
Oh, you're a deal younger

21:19.020 --> 21:21.020
and I figured you'd be prettier too.

21:21.020 --> 21:23.020
Thank you.

21:23.020 --> 21:25.020
I'm awfully sorry about losing my temper

21:25.020 --> 21:27.020
when you called.

21:27.020 --> 21:29.020
Oh, now, now, I understand.

21:29.020 --> 21:31.020
A woman works hard all day cooking

21:31.020 --> 21:33.020
and doing for others.

21:33.020 --> 21:35.020
Young man is hanging on her apron

21:35.020 --> 21:37.020
and she gets a man waspish.

21:37.020 --> 21:39.020
And you're not having a husband to help.

21:39.020 --> 21:41.020
Yes, that's right. I don't have a husband.

21:41.020 --> 21:43.020
How many young did you got?

21:43.020 --> 21:45.020
Youngins.

21:45.020 --> 21:47.020
Uh, well, let's see.

21:47.020 --> 21:49.020
Seven.

21:49.020 --> 21:51.020
Seven?

21:51.020 --> 21:53.020
You must be from our part of the country.

21:53.020 --> 21:55.020
Got started young, didn't you?

21:55.020 --> 21:57.020
Well, come on.

21:57.020 --> 21:59.020
Grandi'll be wanting to meet you.

21:59.020 --> 22:01.020
She's out in the kitchen.

22:01.020 --> 22:03.020
I got you, you big old rascal.

22:03.020 --> 22:05.020
Now you're coming into the house

22:05.020 --> 22:07.020
to help you to get.

22:07.020 --> 22:09.020
And then you're going into the stew.

22:09.020 --> 22:15.020
You're going.

22:15.020 --> 22:17.020
Oh, that's Mr. Tinsman at the back door.

22:17.020 --> 22:19.020
He's my boss.

22:19.020 --> 22:21.020
Come in, come in. I'm Jack Clampett.

22:21.020 --> 22:23.020
A real pleasure, Mr. Clampett.

22:23.020 --> 22:25.020
I'm Bill Tinsman.

22:25.020 --> 22:27.020
I hope everything has been straightened out

22:27.020 --> 22:29.020
and that Beverly Caterers will always be welcome

22:29.020 --> 22:31.020
in your home.

22:31.020 --> 22:33.020
Why, you bet you're lying.

22:33.020 --> 22:35.020
There's a mighty fine young woman.

22:35.020 --> 22:37.020
She says you're her boss.

22:37.020 --> 22:39.020
Beverly Caterers.

22:39.020 --> 22:41.020
Dickens, you say?

22:41.020 --> 22:43.020
Can you do that out here?

22:43.020 --> 22:45.020
Why, of course.

22:45.020 --> 22:47.020
Oh, uh, Mr. Dreisil

22:47.020 --> 22:49.020
holds a small mortgage.

22:49.020 --> 22:51.020
But as soon as that's paid off, she's all mine.

22:51.020 --> 22:53.020
Well, that don't take the ham

22:53.020 --> 22:55.020
off the hog.

22:55.020 --> 22:57.020
Jack, Jack!

22:57.020 --> 22:59.020
Now Jack, you can see I ain't

22:59.020 --> 23:01.020
made it no jug.

23:01.020 --> 23:03.020
Uh, these folks is Beverly Caterers

23:03.020 --> 23:05.020
and Bill Tinsman.

23:05.020 --> 23:07.020
How you cookin'?

23:07.020 --> 23:09.020
I hope we can cook for you, Granny.

23:09.020 --> 23:11.020
You can commence with this one.

23:11.020 --> 23:13.020
I caught him, now you can cook him.

23:13.020 --> 23:15.020
Why, you little

23:15.020 --> 23:17.020
armature.

23:17.020 --> 23:19.020
Untie my giant jack rabbit.

23:19.020 --> 23:21.020
Giant jack rabbit?

23:21.020 --> 23:23.020
Yes, my giant

23:23.020 --> 23:25.020
jack rabbit.

23:25.020 --> 23:27.020
That's what I wanted you to cook for me.

23:27.020 --> 23:29.020
He stands about five foot tall.

23:29.020 --> 23:31.020
Has brown eyes and a

23:31.020 --> 23:33.020
pocket right here.

23:33.020 --> 23:35.020
Go away, I'll go get him for you.

23:35.020 --> 23:37.020
We'll be back directly.

23:37.020 --> 23:39.020
You all go into parlor and let that little fella play

23:39.020 --> 23:41.020
pie and eat for you.

23:45.020 --> 23:47.020
You say eccentric,

23:47.020 --> 23:49.020
I still say nuts.

23:49.020 --> 23:51.020
I say you're right. Let's get out of here.

23:51.020 --> 23:53.020
I don't understand it.

23:53.020 --> 23:55.020
He was free, why should he return?

23:55.020 --> 23:57.020
Something must have frightened him.

23:57.020 --> 23:59.020
I'll say, if he prefers this crate

23:59.020 --> 24:01.020
to freedom. What could it have been?

24:01.020 --> 24:03.020
Hello, over there.

24:03.020 --> 24:05.020
Yes, Granny, what is it?

24:05.020 --> 24:07.020
You see anything of a jack rabbit?

24:07.020 --> 24:09.020
No, we haven't.

24:09.020 --> 24:11.020
You won't find any jack rabbits in Beverly Hills, Granny.

24:11.020 --> 24:13.020
I'll telephone the zoo, sir.

24:13.020 --> 24:15.020
I say,

24:15.020 --> 24:17.020
there's a giant jack rabbit around here

24:17.020 --> 24:19.020
someplace and I'm gonna find him if it's the last

24:19.020 --> 24:21.020
thing I ever know.

24:21.020 --> 24:23.020
Sure you are, Granny. Now come here and lay down.

24:23.020 --> 24:25.020
I'm gonna get that nice Beverly caterer to make a pool just for you here.

24:25.020 --> 24:27.020
Granny, Granny, you caught

24:27.020 --> 24:29.020
something in your snire.

24:29.020 --> 24:31.020
I didn't want it to take.

24:31.020 --> 24:33.020
What'd you catch, Ellie?

24:33.020 --> 24:35.020
Chetro.

24:35.020 --> 24:37.020
Hey, Uncle Chet, put me down.

24:37.020 --> 24:39.020
Uncle Chet, put me down.

24:39.020 --> 24:59.020
Put me down.

24:59.020 --> 25:01.020
Well now it's time to say goodbye

25:01.020 --> 25:03.020
to Chet and all his kin.

25:03.020 --> 25:05.020
They would like to thank you folks

25:05.020 --> 25:07.020
for kindly dropping in.

25:07.020 --> 25:09.020
We're all invited back next week to this locality

25:09.020 --> 25:11.020
to have a heaping helping of their hospitality.

25:11.020 --> 25:13.020
Hell, Vinnie, that is.

25:13.020 --> 25:15.020
Set a spare.

25:15.020 --> 25:17.020
Take your shoes off.

25:17.020 --> 25:37.020
Y'all come back now, yeah?

